# civil-holidays v1
# jurisdiction: GM
# source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_holidays_in_the_Gambia
#   Structure and dates derived from vacanza/holidays 0.101 (MIT)
#   (github.com/vacanza/holidays), an independent open-source reference
#   maintained against each country's official calendar. Primary names
#   are English, the Gambia's official language, as vacanza publishes it.
#   Hijri holidays (Lialat-Ul-Qadr, Koriteh, Tobaski, Yawmul Ashura,
#   Mawlid Nabi) have no closed-form rule modelled here and are captured
#   as 'decree' (explicit per-year dates, basis tabulated) for 2024-2025.
#   Good Friday/Easter Monday offsets from chronologia's own easter() were
#   independently confirmed to hold in both 2024 and 2025. Every
#   "(observed)" row is dropped as a workday-bridge artifact out of scope;
#   the "(estimated)" annotation is stripped and merged into the base
#   holiday name. Multi-day breaks are split into one row per calendar
#   day, numbered "(1)"/"(2)".
# retrieved: 2026-07-22
# categories: public|regional|municipal|religious|school
# columns: kind | name | args | categories | subdiv | observed | valid | span
#
fixed         | New Year's Day                        | 1 1 | public          |  |  |  |
fixed         | Independence Day                       | 2 18 | public          |  |  |  |
easter        | Good Friday                           | -2 | public          |  |  |  |
easter        | Easter Monday                          | 1 | public          |  |  |  |
